// Lesson 4.5 — The Jump: Getting the Player Off the Ground
// Scaffolding: FULL WALKTHROUGH (level 1). A jump has no precedent anywhere in
// the course — the student has moved a transform (1.4), set a velocity (2.2) and
// read a key (1.4), but has never changed a body's momentum in one instant. So
// every line is given and explained, and the lesson is about WHERE each line
// goes and WHY the push is an impulse rather than a force.
//
// GROUND TRUTH (read from the teacher's project — Assets/Scripts/PlayerController.cs):
//   - The same Player prefab is played in two worlds, and the SCRIPT decides
//     which one it woke up in from the scene's NAME:
//         Scene currentScene = SceneManager.GetActiveScene();
//         if (currentScene.name == "Overworld") { rb.gravityScale = 0; isPlatformer = false; }
//         else { rb.gravityScale = 1; isPlatformer = true; ... }
//     `isPlatformer` is a plain private bool, NOT serialized. The old version of
//     this page told the student to declare a serialized flag and tick it in the
//     Inspector; the project does not do that, and no scene carries such an
//     override any more. The page teaches the build's mechanism.
//   - The jump key is J: `Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.J)`, inside `if (isPlatformer)`.
//     Space is the projectile key in this project, not the jump key.
//   - `jumpForce` is `[SerializeField] float jumpForce;` — no initializer; the
//     value 7 lives on Player.prefab and is read from the Inspector. The page
//     makes the student set it there, because a serialized field with no
//     initializer jumps with 0 until they do.
//   - `void Jump()` prints "jump" and calls
//     `rb.AddForceY(jumpForce, ForceMode2D.Impulse);`
//     (Unity 6's axis shorthands; `rb.linearVelocity` is the Unity 6 name.)
//   - In the cave the player moves with `rb.linearVelocityX = xVector;` — gravity
//     owns Y. Writing the full vector would erase the fall every frame. The hub
//     keeps `rb.linearVelocity = new Vector2(xVector, yVector);` from 2.2.
//   - Player.prefab carries no Rigidbody2D and no Collider2D of its own; the
//     student added them in 2.1, where Gravity Scale was set to 0.
//   - Scene names: Start, Overworld, Platformer. The string compared in code is
//     the scene's NAME, not its file path.
//
// PROTECTED BLOCKS — ids are POSITIONAL and persisted. One decompose block with
// THREE turns (4.5:dc1:q1..q3) and one Socratic with THREE questions
